Z||000004||fiero56||06-07-2001||01:55 PM||||If you want to get ripped off at a salvage yard, try out Riverside Auto Salvage in West Carrolton in Ohio. OMG, my mouth drops open everytime they tell me the price for the stuff in my hands. They charge $25 per wiring harnes connector. I asked how much for power mirror heads, and they wanted $70/side. I haven't been there in a long time, don't plan to go back either. But they always have at least a dozen Fieros there, and Fieros there never seem to get picked over much.||||reg||1
Z||000005||The Fieromaster||06-07-2001||02:01 PM||||Dude you guys need to call me or somthing do you know what i payed for a 5 speed Beretta trans (thought i could use it on Fiero) $100 and for a tail light like $5 for the Fiero... IHI turbo... that was about $50 hehehe! I RULE!  Its the people in Northern Ohio.. The junkyards just give away Fiero stuff! Shame on you for taking door emblems... I... uh... Ive.. never done that.. uh...yea..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> LOL!<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.askfelons.com/fieromaster/fieromastergif1.gif">   <BR>~In Memory Of Jesse Cesek~ 1980-2000<BR>1985 GT ~Purple, Black and Yellow Interior(Fastback Converted)<BR>1997 Mitsu Eclipse GSX (AWD, Turbo) DOA on 12/10/2000||||reg||10
Z||000006||rogergarrison||06-07-2001||02:20 PM||||In my body shop, ive learned to check on new parts first. A mid 80 chrys minivan tailite is $17 new aftermarket. I priced a used caddy late model bumper from yard for $750 complete, used (4 parts) Found out new OEM from caddy dealer all 4 parts new were $550. You got a bargin on tach, my local yard wanted $50 and I told em to keep it, i only needed the needle.||||reg||1
