Z||000010||Toddster||06-07-2001||03:20 PM||||This is going to sound kinda obvious but try it. It always seems to work for me.<P>I go to the local Pick&Pull all the time. I scavange lots of odds and ends when I buy something specific. <P>When you go to pay, SMILE. I kid you not. I smile and joke around with the guy at the counter. Once he enters the "whatever I came to buy", then I say, "OH Yeah, here are a couple of odds and ends" (like a tach, escucheon, etc.) They often just say, "Oh, keep it". I've been given free t-shirts, '88 GT horn buttons, badges, heat shields, steering wheels, and other great stuff. All for just being freindly and using good timing. <P>Hey, it doesn't cost a damn thing to do it. It doesn't always work but, more often than not, it does.||||reg||1
Z||000011||Oreif||06-07-2001||03:24 PM||||    <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by The Fieromaster:<BR><B>I CAN use it?  but we looked at everything and all the linkage pieces are backwards and the place the clutch slave goes through is ALL wrong.. like way way wrong??<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Rodney Dickman sells a kit so you can use other 5-spd getrag's in a Fiero.<BR>Look under the "Transaxle" tab at: <A HREF="http://www.rodneydickman.com/retail.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.rodneydickman.com/retail.html</A> <P>Or go right to: <A HREF="http://www.rodneydickman.com/n11.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.rodneydickman.com/n11.html</A> <P><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 06-07-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000012||Ken Wittlief||06-07-2001||03:50 PM||||last time I went to buy something specific at a junk yard, I think it was a tail light for a beetle, the owner pulls out an official VW price book, looks up the retail price, and charges me half - that was their standard price, half of new/retail.<P>  it was also the last time I went there.<P>  when I lived in cedar rapids iowa there was a GREAT junk yard near there, Green Acres.<P>  from time to time on summer weekends they had special all-you-can-carry-for-$20 sales. You go in with your tool box, spend all day in there, and everytime you walk through the gate with their stuff its $20 (they dont charge you to carry your tool box back out).<P>   If two of you can carry a V8 out in your arms, its $40, or a tranny, or a door, anything.<P> if you can drag it out yourself, its $20!<P>   now I wish I lived nearby - there are a ton of things I could get, little stuff, for my '85se - $20! what a deal!<P>   they had a great radio ad parody of the Green Acres TV show song too, some lady that sounded like Eva Gardener, esp the one line:<BR>"Darwling I love you but fix my broken car!"||||reg||1
Z||000013||Ken Wittlief||06-07-2001||03:56 PM||||I should clarify, its not $20 for any one thing, its $20 for everything you can carry all at once<P>  the last time I was there I found audi door handles that replaced the snapoff plastic ones on my rabbit, I think a rear seat for a superbeetle, a steeringwheel, and some VW odds and ends, and on the way out I find a perfect michelin tire on a rabbit rim.<P>  I got it all out in one (slow) staggering pass through the gate - $20 thank you and come again.||||reg||1
Z||000014||qwikgta||06-07-2001||11:36 PM||||Fieromaster, TGOwens is correct, you can use it.  I guy in my club just did up a beretta Getrag on a 98 GP 3800.  Some minor mods to the slave cly area and Rodney D-mans parts worked just fine.  <P>Rob<P>------------------<BR>qwikgta@yahoo.com<BR>88 T-Top coupe, 65K, Header no Cat, 16" GTZ rims, short shifter, swaybar, open element air cleaner, hood vents.<BR>http://robsfieroproject.homestead.com/index.html<BR>http://vafiero.com||||reg||1
