Z||000017||DecadenceR||06-08-2001||09:31 AM||||HAHA...<BR>That's like my friend...<BR>He took 3 of is with him one time, (it was a $10 per person admission) and we took 2 bumpers, a rear seat, tail lights, and rear hatch off of an older (82+ style) camaro. Plus of course the little odds and ends like screws and clips and dash pieces we had in our pockets.<BR>We just flipped the hatch upside down, loaded everything on, and carried it out.||||reg||1
Z||000018||turbo86se||06-08-2001||11:27 AM||||I've never liked those yards that won't let you roam yourself, an employee must go with you and remove parts. I like to get out there myself and remove parts myself, it's a learning process. <P>Several years ago when I was getting a manifold for my 85 coupe from a local yard in MD, they had a slighly wrecked fastback GT near their office. An employee had to go with you, and they wouldn't let anyone near that car, and wanted an insane amount of money for the parts. For some reason I felt they were guarding that car.||||reg||13
